    82	
    83	### Authoritative-source pattern
    84	
    85	SPEC/v1 ships schemas in **two compatible patterns**; the front-matter
    86	declares which:
    87	
    88	| Pattern | Header field | Examples | Meaning |
    89	|---|---|---|---|
    90	| **Mirror** | `Normative source: <path>` | `audit-log.schema.md`, `plan.schema.md`, `debate.schema.md`, `skill-frontmatter.schema.md`, `hook-io.schema.md` | The schema mirrors a repo-internal authoritative source; external drift is an error. |
    91	| **Self-authoritative** | `Normative source: SELF` | `tier-policy.schema.md`, `tournament-report.schema.md`, `rag-sidecar.schema.md`, `predict-budget.schema.md`, `memory-shared.schema.md`, 18+ others | This file IS the authority; there is no internal document paired with it. |
    92	
    93	Both patterns carry equal contract weight. The difference is internal:
    94	mirror schemas track an authoritative doc inside the repo; self-
    95	authoritative schemas track external consumer-facing contracts only.
    96	ADR-007 §Scope documents when each applies.
    97	
    98	Adopters reading the SPEC contract surface do not need to distinguish
    99	the two — every `*.schema.md` file is a published contract. The
   100	frontmatter distinction is for CI drift-checks (mirror-pattern
   101	schemas get a bidirectional drift test; self-authoritative schemas
   102	do not).
   103	
   104	## SemVer contract
   105	
   106	The Compliance SPEC is versioned with **SemVer 2.0.0**. The SPEC version
   107	is in `VERSION` at repo root. Adopters pin their local install to a SPEC
   108	version via `upgrade.sh --pin v1.x.y`.
   109	
   110	### What counts as MAJOR (breaking)
   111	
   112	- Removing or renaming a field in any schema
   113	- Changing a hook I/O shape (input field names, decision JSON keys)
   114	- Changing audit-log event discriminators (`action`, `event_schema`)
   115	- Removing an `install.sh` flag or changing its argument semantics
   116	- Removing an `action` literal from the audit-log v2 known set
   117	- Increasing minimum Python version
   118	
   119	### What counts as MINOR (additive)
   120	
   121	- Adding an optional field to any schema
   122	- Adding a new hook (default-off or fail-open)
   123	- Adding a new archetype to team.md
   124	- Adding a new skill or skill tier
   125	- Adding a new `install.sh` flag
   126	- Adding a new `action` literal to the audit-log v2 known set (requires a new ADR)
   127	
   128	### What counts as PATCH (non-behavioral)
   129	
   130	- Bug fixes that preserve observable behavior
   165	  `parse_error` or any synthesized adapter-only field.
   166	- Environment variables holding credentials (`OPENAI_API_KEY`,
   167	  `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, etc.) are **read-nowhere** by
   168	  adapters. Adapters receive the full payload from stdin; the host
   169	  IDE, not the adapter, authenticated the upstream LLM call.
   170	
   171	---
   172	
   173	## 5. Versioning and deprecation
   174	
   175	### 5.1 Adapter-level versioning
   176	
   177	Each adapter carries its own `ADAPTER_VERSION`. The framework version
   178	(`VERSION=1.3.0-rc.1`) is independent.
   179	
   180	### 5.2 Compatibility
   181	
   182	Within SPEC v1:
   183	- Adding a new adapter is always safe.
   184	- Adding a new field to `CAPABILITIES` is safe.
   185	- Adding a new field to `NormalizedEvent` (per `normalized_envelope.schema.md`)
   378	On server startup, if any handler is within 30 days of its removal
   379	date, server emits `mcp_handler_deprecated_warning` (reserved; not
   380	yet implemented — Sprint 14+).
   381	
   382	---
   383	
   384	## 8. Versioning
   385	
   386	### 8.1 Server version field
   387	
   388	`SERVER_VERSION` constant in `server.py` and
   389	`server_capabilities.py`. Reported via `server.capabilities` result
   390	in `server_version` field. Tracks SemVer of the MCP server
   391	implementation — independent from framework `VERSION`
   392	(`1.4.0-rc.1`) and MCP protocol version (`2024-11-05`).
   393	
   394	### 8.2 Protocol version field
   395	
   396	`PROTOCOL_VERSION` constant in `server_capabilities.py`
   397	(`"2024-11-05"`). Reported via `server.capabilities` result in
   398	`protocol_version` field. Tracks the Model Context Protocol spec
   399	release this server implements.
   400	
   318	### 9.2 RC holds (per ADR-007)
   319	
   320	- `1.0.0-rc.1` is the first publication shipping in PLAN-013 Phase
   321	  C.3 (this document).
   322	- `1.0.0` promotion happens when Phase C.2 merges the populated
   323	  mapping AND the 24h RC hold elapses (per ADR-103, which reduced the original ADR-007 7-day window) AND ADR-043 is ACCEPTED.
   324	- Each subsequent MINOR bump MAY use an RC cycle at the Owner's
   325	  discretion (low-risk additive bumps typically skip RC).
   326	
   327	### 9.3 Relationship to framework VERSION
   328	
   329	The framework `VERSION=1.4.0-rc.1` and this schema `1.0.0-rc.1` are
   330	**independent**. The framework can bump without this schema bumping;
   331	this schema can bump (adding new gap annotations, for instance)
   332	without the framework bumping.
   333	
