     1	# SPEC v1 — state-stores.schema
     2	
     3	> **Normative source:** `.claude/hooks/_lib/state_store.py` (reference driver)
     4	> **Spec version:** 1.0.0-rc.1 (PLAN-011 Phase 0, 2026-04-14)
     5	> **Related ADR:** ADR-027 — Unified Agent State Backend
     6	
     7	## Summary (normative)
     8	
     9	Plan-scoped, redaction-enforced key/value stores used by Sprint-11
    10	surfaces (scratchpad, skill proposals, skill index, session graph) and
    11	any future surface that needs persistent state tied to a `PLAN-NNN`.
    12	
    13	### Envelope
    14	
    15	```
    16	${CEO_STATE_ROOT:-$HOME/.claude/projects/<native-slug>/state}/
    17	    <store_name>/
    18	        <plan_id>.sqlite         # kv storage
    19	        <plan_id>.sqlite.lock    # sibling filelock (fcntl, ADR-002)
    20	        <plan_id>.sqlite-wal     # WAL journal (sqlite-managed)
    21	        <plan_id>.sqlite-shm     # WAL shared memory (sqlite-managed)
    22	```
    23	
    24	### Identifiers
    25	
    26	| Field | Type | Rules |
    27	|---|---|---|
    28	| `store_name` | string | 1–32 chars, `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` only; no slashes/dots |
    29	| `plan_id`    | string | 1–64 chars, `[A-Za-z0-9_.-]`; MUST NOT start with `.`; MUST NOT contain `..` |
    30	| `key`        | string | free-form; length governed by sqlite TEXT PK (1 GB theoretical) |
    31	
    32	Names violating these rules are rejected at `SqliteStateStore.__init__`
    33	with `StateStoreInvalidName`. Validation is **per-argument** — both
    34	`store_name` and `plan_id` are checked.
    35	
    36	### Schema (per-plan sqlite file)
    37	
    38	```sql
    39	CREATE TABLE kv (
    40	    key TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    41	    value BLOB NOT NULL,
    42	    expires_at INTEGER,           -- epoch seconds, NULL = no expiry
    43	    created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,  -- epoch seconds
    44	    redacted INTEGER NOT NULL     -- 1 if redact_secrets changed the original
    45	);
    46	CREATE INDEX idx_kv_expires ON kv(expires_at);
    47	
    48	PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;
    49	PRAGMA synchronous = NORMAL;
    50	PRAGMA temp_store = MEMORY;
    51	```
    52	
    53	Schema additions are MINOR bumps. Column removal / rename is MAJOR
    54	(forbidden within v1). New surfaces SHOULD NOT invent their own
    55	schemas — use the generic `kv` table with structured values (JSON
    56	strings, pickle, etc.) serialized by the caller.
    57	
    58	### Value semantics
    59	
    60	| Input | Pre-write path | Audit field |
    61	|---|---|---|
    62	| `str` | `_lib.redact.redact_secrets(v, max_chars=0)` → UTF-8 bytes | `redaction_applied = (out != in)` |
    63	| `bytes` | trusted; stored as-is | `redaction_applied = false` |
    64	| other | `TypeError` at caller | — |
    65	
    66	Values exceeding `value_max_bytes` (default 64 KiB, per-store-override
    67	allowed) raise `StateStoreValueTooLarge`. **This is NOT fail-open.** A
    68	caller asking for a cap violation means the cap is wrong for that
    69	surface — raise in code, not at audit.
    70	
    71	### TTL semantics
    72	
    73	- `ttl_seconds=None` → never expires
    74	- `ttl_seconds>0` → expires at `now() + ttl_seconds`
    75	- `ttl_seconds<=0` → `ValueError` at `set()`
    76	- Reads on expired keys return `None` and emit `state_store_read` with
    77	  `found=false`. The row is NOT deleted by `get()` — callers must run
    78	  `prune_expired()` on a schedule (typically after session close or
    79	  via an admin tool).
    80	
    81	### Plan rollback semantics
    82	
    83	When a plan transitions `executing → draft` (rollback), callers SHOULD
    84	invoke `store.clear_plan()` to zero out the per-plan state. This emits
    85	a `state_store_pruned` event. There is no automatic rollback hook at
    86	this layer — the plan-transition hook will call into state_store in a
    87	follow-up sprint.
    88	
    89	### Filelock
    90	
    91	Every mutating method and every read path acquires the sibling filelock
    92	(`<plan_id>.sqlite.lock`) via `_lib.filelock.FileLock`. Timeout default
    93	5.0s — longer than audit_emit (2.5s) because sqlite contention is
    94	expected on bursty scratchpad writes.
    95	
    96	### Audit events
    97	
    98	All three events use `event_schema: "v2"` (additive per ADR-005) and
    99	share the mandatory fields `action`, `store_name`, `plan_id_hash`,
   100	`session_id`, `project`, `ts`, `event_schema`. Nullable `tokens_*`
   101	fields are reserved per the audit-log.schema.md pattern.
   102	
   103	| action | per-action required |
   104	|---|---|
   105	| `state_store_write` | `key_hash`, `value_bytes`, `ttl_seconds` (nullable int), `redaction_applied` (bool) |
   106	| `state_store_read` | `key_hash`, `found` (bool) |
   107	| `state_store_pruned` | `keys_pruned_count` (int) |
   108	
   109	`plan_id_hash` is `sha256(plan_id)[:16]`. `key_hash` is
   110	`sha256(key)[:16]`. Plaintext `plan_id` / `key` is NEVER audited.
   111	
   112	### Fail mode
   113	
   114	- **State-mutating paths (set/delete/clear_plan/prune_expired):**
   115	  exceptions propagate. Filelock timeout → `FileLockTimeout`; sqlite
   116	  corruption → `sqlite3.DatabaseError`. State correctness > observability.
   117	- **Audit emission inside state_store:** fail-open (tries/excepts the
   118	  call). Consistent with ADR-005 (framework never blocks on audit).
   119	
   120	### Permissions
   121	
   122	- `state_root` and per-store dirs: `0o700` (owner-only).
   123	- sqlite files: `0o600` (owner-only). `os.chmod` is best-effort after
   124	  the first `connect()`.
   125	
   126	### Back-compat within v1
   127	
   128	- Fields added to `state_store_*` events → MINOR bump of SPEC.
   129	- Removing / renaming fields → MAJOR bump (forbidden within v1).
   130	- Adding new action literals scoped to state stores → MINOR bump + new
   131	  ADR.
   132	
   133	### Consumer contract
   134	
   135	Consumers MAY build derived views (per-plan size, write rate,
   136	redaction-hit rate) by scanning audit-log for `state_store_*` events.
   137	They MUST:
   138	- Tolerate unknown fields (forward-compat).
   139	- Treat `plan_id_hash` as opaque; do not attempt to reverse.
   140	- Handle `ttl_seconds: null` (no expiry).
   141	
   142	### Version history
   143	
   144	| SPEC version | Source commit | Notes |
   145	|---|---|---|
   146	| 1.0.0-rc.1 | Sprint 11 PLAN-011 Phase 0 | Initial envelope + three `state_store_*` events |
